          "label": "<p>Which national health programme has successfully achieved its disease eliminatio</p>",
          "x": 30,
          "y": 30,
          "width": 40,
          "height": 25,
          "libraryTitle": "Multiple Choice",
          "action": {
            "library": "H5P.MultiChoice 1.16",
            "params": {
              "question": "<p>Which national health programme has successfully achieved its disease elimination target of less than 1 case per 10,000 population at the national level?</p>",
              "answers": [
                {
                  "text": "<div>NI-KSHAY (RNTCP)</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>NI-KSHAY aims for tuberculosis elimination by 2025, ahead of the SDG 2030 target, but India has not yet achieved this goal.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>NVBDCP</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>NVBDCP set a Kala-azar elimination target of &lt;1 per 10,000 by 2023, but the programme covers multiple vector-borne diseases and full national elimination has not been confirmed across all of them.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>NACP (NACO)</div>",
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>NACP focuses on HIV/AIDS control through free ART, ICTC, and PMTCT. It has achieved a decline in new infections but uses different metrics, not the &lt;1/10,000 elimination threshold.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                },
                {
                  "text": "<div>NLEP (National Leprosy Eradication Programme)</div>",
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "<div>India achieved national leprosy elimination (&lt;1 per 10,000) through NLEP's multi-drug therapy — dapsone + rifampicin + clofazimine — combined with active case detection and stigma reduction.</div>",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  }
                }
              ],
              "overallFeedback": [
                {
                  "from": 0,
                  "to": 50,
                  "feedback": "The National Leprosy Eradication Programme (NLEP) achieved <1 per 10,000 nationally using MDT (dapsone + rifampicin + clofazimine). Other programmes like NI-KSHAY and NVBDCP have set similar targets but are still working towards them."
                },
                {
                  "from": 51,
                  "to": 100,
                  "feedback": "Correct! India achieved national leprosy elimination (<1/10,000) through NLEP's MDT regimen — one of the landmark public health achievements."
                }
              ],
